From 7e00d662a1874662c38814427fb46e10281d51e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akif-b-Atif <akif.b.atif@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Weight repeated words/phrases by how spread out across days
 they are

A word/phrase now tracks the distinct days it was said on (per person and
overall); same-day repeats count as one entry while the total count is
still kept. Eligibility requires MIN_REPEAT_DAYS days, scores are weighted
by days / (days + SPREAD_HALF_DAYS) on top of the existing relative
frequency logic, and signature ownership/dominance is decided by day
entries so a one-day burst can't become someone's trademark.

Short slices (last-N-days, arcs) scale the day requirements down. Reports
show the day counts; --min-repeat-days / --spread-half-days override the
defaults. Also dedupes the loosened-profile construction in analyze_chat.
